PianoTorch is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE): piano's rear torch (backlog B12). What it takes from other
work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoUsbHost/PianoUsbHost.cpp (sha256 344da37e70682f579b6c0915ab5ac2e38183b17334b1ed0d883c7d5d6c453415): the kext's shape
    (probe gate on the boot argument, a survey thread, the post-mortem stage word, the SPMI windows mapped uncached and loaded with an
    explicit ldr, one summary property), re-written for this driver.
  package/PianoBacklight/PianoBacklight.cpp (sha256 4483d0384a5e958956d1755ff065b6e3a655eca653b4bd08ce165ce854bfb6d5): the control
    pattern (requests queued under a lock for the service's thread, an administrator-only setProperties, callPlatformFunction entries
    for other drivers, copyMatchingService lookups of other drivers' properties), re-written for this driver.
  package/PianoPower/SpmiObserver.h (sha256 4805d4fb7af91c210d75b9791e125f3789b7671e895afe6f80af27a36a849b07): included, not copied
    (the arbiter v7 windows, the APID map and owner table, the observer read).
  package/PianoDwc3/PianoDwc3.cpp (setRestartReason): the arbiter v7 owner-channel write this repository already makes (chnls +
    0x1000 * APID, data at +0x10, command opcode 0 at +0x00, status at +0x08); re-expressed in TorchCore.h spmiWriteByte.
  package/include/PianoPowerContract.h: the power-tree join and the synchronous off in setPowerState(kOff) (docs/power.md section 4).
  tooling/native/pianousb-shell/pianousb-shell.c (sha256 85b3dca552641fd5089cae0189840f5576c2f2b52c1c3d304b6d2b3241de691a): the form of
    a user-space tool built on the Mac for the tablet's macOS (tooling/native/piano-torch/piano-torch.c).

